# Vercel CLI link state
.vercel

# pyproject.toml + uv.lock are TRACKED on purpose. This REVERSES #53/de081a2,
# whose premise was empirically false: the Vercel Python builder consumes a
# provided uv.lock with `uv sync --frozen` and it takes PRECEDENCE over
# requirements.txt, and `.gitignore` does NOT stop `vercel deploy` from uploading
# local files (only `.vercelignore` does). So "ignore the lock, trust
# requirements.txt" let a STALE LOCAL uv.lock silently ship the wrong engine
# (the 8.1.0->8.2.0 ReDoS-fix miss). The committed, hash-pinned uv.lock +
# pyproject.toml are now the single reproducible source of truth; bump via
# `uv lock --upgrade-package schliff==<ver>` and review the hash diff.
# `!uv.lock` re-includes it past the repo-root global `uv.lock` ignore.
!uv.lock
